* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* MVSMF -- route definitions for the httpd parmlib member (DD:HTTPPRM)
*
* Add these four lines to the member your HTTPD started task names on
* its //HTTPPRM DD. They are the same four that ship in httpd's own
* samplib(HTTPPRM0); keep the two in step.
*
* ORDER MATTERS -- FIRST MATCH WINS. The three specific routes must come
* before the /zosmf/* catch-all, or the catch-all swallows them.
*
* AUTH=NONE on the first two is not a hole. Both endpoints resolve the
* caller themselves and answer 401 without a credential:
*
*   /zosmf/info                  authenticated like every other route
*                                since #324 -- the "anonymous liveness
*                                probe" it was once documented as never
*                                existed, and the reference gates its
*                                own /zosmf/info too
*   /zosmf/services/authenticate the token login. A failed login has no
*                                ACEE and still has to reach the handler
*                                to get the z/OSMF-shaped 401 body, so
*                                httpd must not gate it
*
* The third route is the console service, which has a profile check of its own:
*
*   /zosmf/restconsoles/*        issues operator commands and checks
*                                nobody's authority itself, so httpd
*                                checks READ on the RAKF resource
*                                FACILITY MVSMF.CONSOLE. Define it
*                                (docs/installation.md, step 4): with no
*                                profile the check permits everyone and
*                                HTTPD425W says so at startup. Listed
*                                after /zosmf/* it is never reached --
*                                silently.
*
* A route line with no AUTH= at all reads as AUTH=NONE (public) in
* /.dsrv?target=MOD. That is a poor thing for an audit to find, which is
* why all four say what they mean.
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
MOD=MVSMF /zosmf/info                    AUTH=NONE
MOD=MVSMF /zosmf/services/authenticate   AUTH=NONE
MOD=MVSMF /zosmf/restconsoles/*          AUTH=TOKEN RES=FACILITY:MVSMF.CONSOLE
MOD=MVSMF /zosmf/*                       AUTH=TOKEN
*
* To narrow access further, protect the catch-all with a resource check
* instead of widening the prefix:
*
* MOD=MVSMF /zosmf/*  AUTH=TOKEN RES=FACILITY:MVSMF.ACCESS
